  "narration": [
    {
      "segment": "title",
      "start": 0.4,
      "end": 5.2,
      "text": "Welcome. In this short lesson we will find out what happens when an acid meets a base."
    },
    {
      "segment": "ppe",
      "start": 6.3,
      "end": 10.311,
      "text": "Before any experiment, put on a lab coat, gloves and safety goggles."
    },
    {
      "segment": "ppe",
      "start": 10.661,
      "end": 13.69,
      "text": "Acids and bases can damage your skin and eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment": "acid_base",
      "start": 14.8,
      "end": 17.189,
      "text": "Here a scientist pours a solution in the lab."
    },
    {
      "segment": "acid_base",
      "start": 17.539,
      "end": 22.297,
      "text": "An acid such as hydrochloric acid releases hydrogen ions in water."
    },
    {
      "segment": "acid_base",
      "start": 22.647,
      "end": 26.828,
      "text": "A base such as sodium hydroxide releases hydroxide ions."
    },
    {
      "segment": "reaction",
      "start": 27.933,
      "end": 33.779,
      "text": "When the two solutions are mixed, each hydrogen ion joins a hydroxide ion to form water."
    },
    {
      "segment": "reaction",
      "start": 34.129,
      "end": 38.929,
      "text": "The sodium and chloride ions that remain make table salt, which stays dissolved."
    },
    {
      "segment": "indicator",
      "start": 40.033,
      "end": 42.828,
      "text": "An indicator shows when the reaction is complete."
    },
    {
      "segment": "indicator",
      "start": 43.178,
      "end": 47.317,
      "text": "Universal indicator turns green at pH seven, which is neutral."
    },
    {
      "segment": "hazard",
      "start": 48.433,
      "end": 50.225,
      "text": "Accidents can happen in any lab."
    },
    {
      "segment": "hazard",
      "start": 50.575,
      "end": 54.117,
      "text": "If glassware breaks, never pick up the sharp pieces with your hands."
    },
    {
      "segment": "hazard",
      "start": 54.467,
      "end": 57.603,
      "text": "Tell your teacher and sweep them up with a brush and dustpan."
    },
    {
      "segment": "summary",
      "start": 58.733,
      "end": 61.827,
      "text": "So, an acid plus a base gives a salt plus water."
    },
    {
      "segment": "summary",
      "start": 62.177,
      "end": 68.022,
      "text": "This reaction is called neutralization, and antacid tablets use it to settle an upset stomach."
    }
  ],
